00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:04,940
rolled and blended for several hours to a smooth consistency,

520
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:12,820
a process stumbled upon by this company's founder back in 1879.

521
00:33:12,821 --> 00:33:15,220
While experimenting with chocolate blending techniques

522
00:33:15,320 --> 00:33:19,220
in his shop, Rudolf Lindt took off for a hunting weekend

523
00:33:19,320 --> 00:33:22,160
and accidentally forgot to shut off his mechanical rolling

524
00:33:22,260 --> 00:33:22,960
machine.

525
00:33:25,260 --> 00:33:28,560
He returned to find his chocolate had a velvety texture

526
00:33:28,660 --> 00:33:31,080
and a flavor superior to previous incarnations.

527
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:36,880
The modern-day conch has evolved into the workhorse of any

528
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:38,020
chocolate factory.

529
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:41,680
In the past, it was with water mills driven,

530
00:33:41,681 --> 00:33:45,680
Later on, it was driven with steam engine.

531
00:33:45,681 --> 00:33:50,680
Today, we have machines with the capacity from 13,000 pounds

532
00:33:50,681 --> 00:33:57,680
and with a huge, powerful motor that can create up to 1,800 RPMs.

533
00:33:57,681 --> 00:34:00,680
And everything is computer-controlled.

534
00:34:00,681 --> 00:34:04,680
The temperatures are controlled, the speed is controlled.

535
00:34:04,681 --> 00:34:07,680
You can run clockwise, you can run anti-clockwise,

536
00:34:07,681 --> 00:34:09,680
you're adding cocoa batteries,

537
00:34:09,681 --> 00:34:12,580
You have about 20 to 30 different steps

538
00:34:12,680 --> 00:34:16,780
in the inside of the conch.

539
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:20,520
After conching, the chocolate is molded into hollow orbs.

540
00:34:20,620 --> 00:34:24,420
We're filling one half of the mold set with chocolate.

541
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:26,900
We're putting on the top half of the mold set,

542
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,800
and then we're going through a series of three rotations,

543
00:34:29,900 --> 00:34:32,640
gently swirling the chocolate around the inside

544
00:34:32,740 --> 00:34:34,100
of the mold cavity.

545
00:34:34,200 --> 00:34:38,000
And by doing so, we're creating a hollow sphere.

546
00:34:38,001 --> 00:34:43,240
Once the shells have cooled and hardened, in goes the filling,

547
00:34:43,340 --> 00:34:45,240
topped off with a dab of chocolate

548
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:46,740
to make sure nothing leaks out.

549
00:34:51,740 --> 00:34:54,720
What makes the secret chocolate filling recipe unique

550
00:34:54,820 --> 00:34:59,160
is that lint has found a way to lower its melting point,

551
00:34:59,260 --> 00:35:01,520
creating a cooling sensation in your mouth.

552
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:06,700
Lindor truffles may taste expensive,

553
00:35:06,701 --> 00:35:08,740
but Lindt's ability to mass produce them

554
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:11,600
ensures that premium chocolate won't send you to the poorhouse.

555
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:19,240
Good thing, too, because there's about to be a mad rush for

556
00:35:19,340 --> 00:35:20,940
chocolate.

557
00:35:21,040 --> 00:35:25,520
It's been several hundred years, but real chocoholism is back,

558
00:35:25,620 --> 00:35:30,220
not the candy store kind, but the Aztec obsession kind,

559
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:33,820
minus the human sacrifices.

560
00:35:33,821 --> 00:35:36,760
The future for chocolate will come from its past.

561
00:35:36,820 --> 00:35:39,600
We're really trying to understand the history.

562
00:35:39,660 --> 00:35:42,220
We're trying to understand the agronomy.

563
00:35:42,300 --> 00:35:45,940
We're trying to understand the molecular chemistry,

564
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,960
the genes of cocoa.

565
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:52,040
True chocolate lovers are searching out fine flavor

566
00:35:52,100 --> 00:35:55,480
chocolate made with high quality beans.

567
00:35:55,540 --> 00:35:57,880
They're learning about origin cocoa.

568
00:35:57,940 --> 00:36:01,140
Cocoa from Madagascar tastes different than cocoa

569
00:36:01,220 --> 00:36:03,820
from Ecuador.

570
00:36:03,821 --> 00:36:06,620
They're looking at percentages on cocoa on the bars that they

571
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:07,420
buy.

572
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:12,560
The percentage noted on chocolate products

573
00:36:12,660 --> 00:36:15,060
refers to the amount of chocolate liquor,

574
00:36:15,160 --> 00:36:16,460
plus any added cocoa butter.

575
00:36:19,800 --> 00:36:24,140
From a medical perspective, dark chocolate, 60% and higher,

576
00:36:24,240 --> 00:36:26,500
is all the rage.

577
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,280
Step aside, spinach.

578
00:36:28,380 --> 00:36:31,020
There's a new health food in town.

579
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:33,380
There's more and more evidence of late

580
00:36:33,381 --> 00:36:37,880
that dark chocolate is one of those rare foods

581
00:36:37,980 --> 00:36:43,860
that is a great indulgence that's actually good for us.

582
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:48,120
Dark chocolate is the most concentrated source

583
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:51,700
of antioxidants readily available to us in our diets,

584
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,700
more concentrated than green tea,

585
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:59,400
more concentrated than virtually all fruits and vegetables.

586
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:02,040
And in particular, the family of antioxidants

587
00:37:02,041 --> 00:37:06,040
in dark chocolate called flavonoids are associated

588
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:09,680
with reduced risk of heart disease, reduced risk of injury

589
00:37:09,780 --> 00:37:14,080
to blood vessels, reduced risk of diabetes, reduced risk

590
00:37:14,180 --> 00:37:17,780
of stroke, reduced risk of cancer.

591
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:21,000
So is dark chocolate really a miracle food?

592
00:37:21,100 --> 00:37:23,700
Too much of even a good thing is not necessarily

593
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:24,900
a good thing.

594
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:28,500
And we know in medicine that the dose makes the poison.

595
00:37:28,501 --> 00:37:32,300
And chocolate, for all of its beneficial health effects,

596
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:35,840
it's a concentrated source of calories.

597
00:37:35,940 --> 00:37:39,540
Consider the health benefits icing on the chocolate king.

598
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:41,980
Because good for you or not, people

599
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:45,020
will continue their love affair with chocolate,

600
00:37:45,120 --> 00:37:46,520
especially during the holidays.

601
00:37:52,220 --> 00:37:56,900
For chocolate lovers, any time is a good time,

602
00:37:56,901 --> 00:38:01,700
especially holiday time, Easter, Christmas,

603
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:06,280
and don't be caught dead without some on Valentine's Day.

604
00:38:06,380 --> 00:38:08,680
If it's not a Hershey or Mars product,

605
00:38:08,780 --> 00:38:10,180
odds are you're enjoying something

606
00:38:10,280 --> 00:38:14,660
made of the R.M. Palmer Company of Reading, Pennsylvania,

607
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:17,260
the number one producer of holiday chocolate treats

608
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:20,060
for over half a century.

609
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:21,120
Take Easter.

610
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:26,000
Each year, the R.M. Palmer Company

611
00:38:26,001 --> 00:38:29,200
makes about 200 million chocolate Easter bunnies

612
00:38:29,300 --> 00:38:32,500
in all shapes and sizes.

613
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:34,840
Both the chocolate Easter bunny and the chocolate egg

614
00:38:34,940 --> 00:38:39,240
go back to Germany in the 1700s.

615
00:38:39,340 --> 00:38:42,440
The bunny and the egg symbolized fertility.

616
00:38:42,540 --> 00:38:45,960
And spring, as we know, is the rebirth of nature

617
00:38:46,060 --> 00:38:47,660
and everything that goes with it.

618
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:53,500
So the Germans associated these two icons with Easter.

619
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:55,100
To capitalize on the craze,

620
00:38:55,101 --> 00:38:58,100
R.M. Palmer Sr. devised a way to make hollow chocolate

621
00:38:58,200 --> 00:39:04,100
Easter bunnies with an unusual ingredient,

622
00:39:04,200 --> 00:39:06,440
personality.

623
00:39:06,540 --> 00:39:10,440
Our company was started by my father, Richard Palmer Sr.,

624
00:39:10,540 --> 00:39:12,760
in 1948.

625
00:39:12,860 --> 00:39:16,560
At that time, all bunnies were more or less traditional.

626
00:39:16,660 --> 00:39:18,060
They looked like this.

627
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:20,760
We made them look like this, which is more of a cartoon

628
00:39:20,860 --> 00:39:21,760
version.

629
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:24,600
This was our first product in 1948.

630
00:39:24,601 --> 00:39:26,580
And actually, it's still in the line today.

631
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:29,040
This bunny and I are exactly the same age.

632
00:39:29,980 --> 00:39:32,260
As a matter of fact, we have exactly the same amount of hair.

633
00:39:33,340 --> 00:39:35,900
The first Palmer bunnies were molded on a machine

634
00:39:35,901 --> 00:39:37,780
designed by the company founder himself.

635
00:39:39,780 --> 00:39:41,480
And it's still going strong.

636
00:39:42,540 --> 00:39:44,980
We're looking at line one here at the R.M. Palmer Company.

637
00:39:45,200 --> 00:39:47,380
We put a polycarbonate mold into the line.

638
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:49,920
We heat it to about 90 to 95 degrees

639
00:39:49,921 --> 00:39:51,860
to ensure that it has a proper release point.

640
00:39:51,861 --> 00:39:55,200
The chocolate's deposited around 84 to 85 degrees,

641
00:39:55,201 --> 00:39:56,400
depending on the product.

642
00:39:56,401 --> 00:39:58,400
We also have to ensure that we have the right viscosity

643
00:39:58,401 --> 00:40:01,500
so we get the proper wall thickness.

644
00:40:01,501 --> 00:40:03,200
The amount of chocolate deposited

645
00:40:03,201 --> 00:40:06,500
is just enough to coat the walls.

646
00:40:06,501 --> 00:40:10,620
The molds rotate a total of 60 times per bunny cycle

647
00:40:10,621 --> 00:40:12,420
to ensure the chocolate is distributed

648
00:40:12,421 --> 00:40:16,420
evenly throughout the cavity, leaving a perfect hollow center.

649
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:21,820
These long-eared big boys are ready to receive

650
00:40:21,821 --> 00:40:24,660
their personas.

651
00:40:24,760 --> 00:40:26,760
And if you've ever wondered...

652
00:40:26,860 --> 00:40:29,220
All of our hollow chocolate bunnies have eyes.

653
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:31,320
The eyes could be yellow, they could be white,

654
00:40:31,420 --> 00:40:33,360
they could be blue, they could be pink.

655
00:40:33,460 --> 00:40:35,760
Most of them, the traditional ones,

656
00:40:35,860 --> 00:40:38,400
are made out of an icing material, which is basically

657
00:40:38,500 --> 00:40:42,680
water, sugar, and egg albumin.

658
00:40:42,780 --> 00:40:46,620
A contemporary cousin of line one, line 10,

659
00:40:46,720 --> 00:40:50,880
produces small bunnies by the army.

660
00:40:50,881 --> 00:40:52,220
It looks pretty simple.

661
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:55,500
Mold goes under depositor.

662
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:58,040
Depositor pours chocolate into mold.

663
00:40:58,880 --> 00:40:59,620
Not quite.

664
00:41:01,680 --> 00:41:04,160
On line 10, it's what you don't see

665
00:41:04,161 --> 00:41:05,780
that makes these bunnies so popular.

666
00:41:06,200 --> 00:41:08,300
This line actually has the capability

667
00:41:08,301 --> 00:41:10,980
of producing almost 80,000 pounds a day.

668
00:41:11,380 --> 00:41:14,500
Today alone, we will make almost 4 million bunnies

669
00:41:14,501 --> 00:41:15,800
coming off of this line,

670
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:17,240
and they're all filled with peanut butter.

671
00:41:17,241 --> 00:41:21,240
A pipe carrying chocolate and a pipe

672
00:41:21,340 --> 00:41:23,880
carrying peanut butter meet at the depositor,

673
00:41:23,980 --> 00:41:28,480
where a central pipe ends in a nozzle inside a nozzle.

674
00:41:28,580 --> 00:41:31,780
The chocolate ejects a hair of a second before the peanut

675
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:35,820
butter and continues for a fraction of a second thereafter.

676
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:38,500
This allows the chocolate to fully encapsulate the peanut

677
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:40,100
butter in the center.

678
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:41,900
First thing you've got to ensure

679
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:45,000
is that the material has the same density and the same

680
00:41:45,001 --> 00:41:47,760
and the same viscosity characteristics

681
00:41:47,761 --> 00:41:50,100
so that they have the correct flow property.

682
00:41:50,600 --> 00:41:52,420
After that, it's strictly mathematics

683
00:41:52,421 --> 00:41:56,000
with piston diameter as well as the channeling

684
00:41:56,001 --> 00:41:57,020
inside the nozzle plate.

685
00:41:57,360 --> 00:42:00,760
Those techniques will ensure a perfect peanut butter center,

686
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:02,780
or as we call a one-shot center,

687
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:04,200
in each and every little bunny.

688
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:08,840
Whether you enjoy them hollow or filled,

689
00:42:09,460 --> 00:42:11,620
everyone knows which part to chomp first.

690
00:42:11,621 --> 00:42:14,960
In fact, 76% of us go straight for the ears.

691
00:42:19,120 --> 00:42:21,460
The experts at Palmer think they know why.

692
00:42:24,260 --> 00:42:26,960
The reason is probably that in the process

693
00:42:27,060 --> 00:42:29,980
of making a hollow bunny, more chocolate goes to the ears

694
00:42:30,080 --> 00:42:31,980
than goes to the rest of the bunny.

695
00:42:32,080 --> 00:42:35,280
So real chocolate lovers would therefore gravitate to the ears,

696
00:42:35,380 --> 00:42:37,880
just like this.

697
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:38,980
Mmm.

698
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:39,980
Great.

699
00:42:39,981 --> 00:42:44,980
So be it bunny or trouble, milk or dark, solid or liquid,

700
00:42:45,080 --> 00:42:49,520
chocolate producers continue to crank out the good stuff.

701
00:42:49,620 --> 00:42:51,660
Maybe that's because manufacturers,

702
00:42:51,760 --> 00:42:55,520
like most everyone else, love their chocolate too.

703
00:42:55,620 --> 00:42:57,360
And a nice flavor.

704
00:42:57,460 --> 00:43:00,660
It's the kind of flavor that you put a piece of chocolate

705
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:04,800
in your mouth, and you just go, mmm.

